tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-396-a-buffer-is-declared-whole.hero:24:41: error[ffi_parameter_type]: `buf` of `setvbuf` cannot be declared `[i8]` — the buffer C is handed lives for this call and no longer, and `buf` is not declared `lent`, so it is taken to keep it — if C keeps the address after the call (`setvbuf`), no buffer of one call can serve it; if it does not, say so: `counted_by 64 lent`
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-396-a-buffer-is-declared-whole.hero:25:29: error[ffi_parameter_type]: `md` of `no_extent` cannot be declared `[u8]` — an array lent through `@` crosses as a buffer exactly as long as its declaration says, and this one states no extent: `@md: [u8] counted_by <n> lent`, the number C writes, a constant of the group, or the sibling that tells C how many
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-396-a-buffer-is-declared-whole.hero:26:28: error[ffi_parameter_type]: `out` of `strings` cannot be declared `[str]` — an array lent through `@` crosses as a buffer C fills, of numbers or of this group's records, and `str` is neither
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-396-a-buffer-is-declared-whole.hero:27:28: error[ffi_parameter_type]: `out` of `handles` cannot be declared `[Handle]` — `Handle` is a handle, a pointer whose life its marks keep, and a buffer of them would hand the program pointers no mark began — a buffer holds numbers or this group's records
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-396-a-buffer-is-declared-whole.hero:28:43: error[counted_by_shape]: `counted_by` on `md` of `nowhere` names no extent — `NOPE` names no other parameter of `nowhere` and no `constant` of its group — the extent is the sibling C reads the count from, a constant the group declares from the header, or the number itself
tests/golden/check/fixedbugs-396-a-buffer-is-declared-whole.hero:29:27: error[ffi_type]: `[u8]` cannot cross the FFI boundary, and it is an `extern`'s parameter — a C header can declare a number, `bool`, `str`, `ptr`, `cstr`, a function type as a parameter, and a `record` declared in this same group (§4.19)
